This vault is managed by `ztlctl`. Treat the MCP surface as canonical when it is available, and use the CLI as the fallback contract.

## Core Rules

- Prefer `ztlctl` workflows over ad hoc markdown editing when content lifecycle matters.
- Use one active session at a time and check `session_status` before starting a new one.
- Search before creating.
- Reuse existing tags via `list_tags` when possible.
- Prefer `ingest_source` for external text, files, and provider-backed URLs when provenance matters.
- Prefer one-step note creation with authored `body`, `key_points`, `aliases`, and `links` when creating synthesis or knowledge notes.
- Run `reweave` after important note creation.
- Use `vault_review` for health checks and periodic reviews.
- Use `draft_from_topic` when a topic packet is strong enough to become a note, task, or decision draft.
- Read `ztlctl://review/dashboard`, `ztlctl://garden/backlog`, and `ztlctl://decision-queue` for enrichment-oriented context.

